<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Big Bear</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1825–1888</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mistahimaskwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Big Bear, Mistahimaskwa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a>, was a Plains Cree chief who long refused to sign Treaty 6 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, holding out for better terms until 1882 as the bison disappeared. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a> of 1885 warriors of his band killed settlers at Frog Lake against his wishes. He surrendered and was imprisoned for treason, and died soon after his release.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/big-bear.jpg" alt="Big Bear" width="320" height="529" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: O.B. Buell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bigbear-blanket.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
